# Change 2: Course Creator Panel Polish, Navigation Fixes & Platform Performance Optimization

Addresses specific usability issues in the Course Creator panel, navigation routing bugs, static demo notification cleanup, and platform-wide performance optimizations while preserving a minimal, lightweight, and user-friendly interface.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Minimalist & User-Friendly UI**: All new features and workflows are kept strictly minimal, non-cluttered, and faithful to the existing design system without adding complex multi-step wizards or visual noise.
> - **Accurate Sidebar Active States**: Ensures exact matching so only the currently active tab is highlighted (e.g. *Student Review Queue* on `/creator/requests`).
> - **Real-Time Dynamic Badges**: Replaces all hardcoded badge numbers (e.g. the static `7`) with live database queries (hidden when count is 0).
> - **Platform Speed & Responsiveness**: Sub-30ms API responses through non-blocking asynchronous backup database replication, warm connection pooling, and client-side data caching.

---

## Proposed Changes for Change 2

### Component 1: Sidebar Navigation & Active Route Highlighting

#### [MODIFY] [client/src/components/layout/AppShell.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/client/src/components/layout/AppShell.jsx)
- **Exact Path Matching**: Fix route matching logic for sidebar navigation items (`location.pathname === item.path`) so parent routes like `/creator` do not stay permanently highlighted when visiting child pages like `/creator/requests` or `/creator/courses`.
- **Dynamic Badge Counts**: Replace hardcoded badge values (`badge: 7`) with dynamic state fetched from live backend endpoints. If pending count is 0, completely omit the badge.
- **Notification Bell Trigger**: Only display the active notification indicator dot if real, unread notifications exist for the authenticated user.

